          "solution": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef fisher_categorical_split(G_cats: np.ndarray, H_cats: np.ndarray, lam: float) -> str:\n    Gc = np.asarray(G_cats, dtype=float)\n    Hc = np.asarray(H_cats, dtype=float)\n    order = np.argsort(Gc / (Hc + lam))\n    G_tot, H_tot = float(Gc.sum()), float(Hc.sum())\n    par_score = (G_tot ** 2) / (H_tot + lam)\n    best_gain, best_left = -1.0, []\n    for k in range(1, len(Gc)):\n        left = order[:k]\n        GL, HL = float(Gc[left].sum()), float(Hc[left].sum())\n        GR, HR = G_tot - GL, H_tot - HL\n        gain = 0.5 * ((GL ** 2) / (HL + lam) + (GR ** 2) / (HR + lam) - par_score)\n        if gain > best_gain:\n            best_gain = gain\n            best_left = sorted(int(i) for i in left)\n    return f'left={best_left},gain={best_gain:.4f}'\n```"
